{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(0)=0 \\\\  & ⋮\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThus, for $n>2,$ we have ${h}^{(n)}(x)=0.$ Listing a few elements of our set, we have the following:\n\n$$\nC={4x,4,0}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|C|=3,$ which is finite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$A$ only.\"" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306604 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306605 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306606 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306607 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306608 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1041 "selection" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1104 #edb/ref 17592186306604 13194139534736 true] [17592186306603 1110 #uuid "89c2cdfd-b450-5a85-9e38-85a64e0cd728" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306604 1034 "$A$ only" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306604 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534736 true] [17592186306604 1111 #uuid "815ed5da-56da-5f68-96ec-10afa7488b14" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306605 1034 "$B$ and $C$ only" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306605 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534736 true] [17592186306605 1111 #uuid "8dd3c35e-5048-5d7c-b69d-6a93ea51d79c" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306606 1034 "$A$ and $B$ only" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306606 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534736 true] [17592186306606 1111 #uuid "fbbf2a60-9e63-5f1a-984b-9722f771c61c" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306607 1034 "$C$ only" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306607 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534736 true] [17592186306607 1111 #uuid "47df099a-22d3-5960-8142-d89de6725a57" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306608 1034 "$B$ only" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306608 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045454 13194139534736 true] [17592186306608 1111 #uuid "e48a4405-6074-57e7-8f6b-393d5cf8475e" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1017 #edb/ref 17592186306610 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1089 "q-181719" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1100 "Which of the following sets are infinite?\n\n- $A={n\\in Z\\,:\\,|3n|<10}$\n- $B={q\\in Q\\,:\\,|3q|<10}$\n- $C={x\\in R\\,:\\,|3x|<10}$" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1113 #uuid "4a5d5c69-dcda-5ac7-93b7-2e058ac5c1f2" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306609 1145 "The cardinality of a finite set is the number of elements contained within it. A set is infinite if it has infinitely many elements. \n\nWe start by solving the following inequality for $x\\in R:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}|3x|<10 \\\\ 3|x|<10 \\\\ |x|<\\frac{10}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhich gives\n\n$$\n-\\frac{10}{3}<x<\\frac{10}{3}\n$$\n\nand can be expressed as $x\\in I=(-\\frac{10}{3},\\frac{10}{3}).$ \n\nWith that in mind, let's examine our sets:\n\n- The set $A$ is finite. If $n\\in Z,$ the solutions to the inequality $|3n|<10$ are all the integers that lie in the interval $I.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\nA={-3,-2,-1,0,1,2,3}.\n$$\n\nConsequently, $|A|=7,$ which is finite.\n\n- The set $B$ is infinite. If $q\\in Q,$ the solutions to $|3q|<10$ are all the rational numbers that lie in the interval $I.$ Since any real interval of nonzero length contains infinitely many rational numbers, it follows that $B$ is infinite.\n\n- The set $C$ is infinite. Since $B$ is infinite, and $B⊂C,$ it follows that $C$ is infinite.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$B$ and $C$ only.\"" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306611 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306612 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306613 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306614 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1000 #edb/ref 17592186306615 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1041 "selection" 13194139534736 true] [17592186306610 1104 #ed